cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this software or its bundled frozen datasets contributed to your work,
  please cite both the software release and the dataset sources listed in
  public/data-catalog.js (NIED K-NET/KiK-net DOI 10.17598/NIED.0004,
  J-SHIS, JMA, GSI, GEBCO 2025 doi:10.5285/37c52e96-24ea-67ce-e063-7086abc05f29).
title: Earthquake Simulator Pro
abstract: >-
  Web-based research-oriented earthquake and tsunami simulation platform for
  Japan: faithful Zhao et al. (2006) GMPE with calibrated bias tables, 1D
  equivalent-linear site response, ensemble uncertainty fields, kinematic
  finite-fault sources (DC3D), two-way AMR nonlinear shallow-water tsunami
  solver with optional Peregrine-type Boussinesq dispersion, EEW inversion
  rehearsal and a real-time monitoring suite. All validation results,
  including negative ones, are frozen in PHYSICS_BENCHMARKS.md.
